#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:2
msgid "Image Builder"
msgstr "Constructor de imágenes"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:4
msgid ""
"The Morpheus Image Builder tool creates vmdk, qcow2, vhd and raw Images "
"from scratch. The Image Builder creates a blank VM in VMware, attaches an"
" os iso, executes a boot script on the VM at startup via VNC which calls "
"a preseed script which runs the unattended os installation and "
"configuration. Morpheus then executes an ova export of the completed vmdk"
" to target Storage provider, and converts the image to all other "
"specified formats. The new Virtual Image records are automatically added "
"to Morpheus and the Images are then available for use."
msgstr ""
"The Morpheus Image Builder tool creates vmdk, qcow2, vhd and raw Images "
"from scratch. The Image Builder creates a blank VM in VMware, attaches an "
"os iso, executes a boot script on the VM at startup via VNC which calls a "
"preseed script which runs the unattended os installation and "
"configuration. Morpheus then executes an ova export of the completed vmdk "
"to target Storage provider, and converts the image to all other specified "
"formats. The new Virtual Image records are automatically added to Morpheus "
"and the Images are then disponible for use."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:7
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr "Requisitos"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:9
msgid ""
"DHCP must be enabled on the network specified for the VM in Morpheus, and"
" network settings configured for DHCP in Morpheus"
msgstr ""
"DHCP debe estar habilitado en la red especificada para la VM en "
"Morpheus, y la configuración de red debe estar configurada para DHCP "
"en Morpheus"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:10
msgid ""
"The blank VM must get network configuration via DHCP upon boot. Static IP"
" assignment is not possible."
msgstr ""
"La VM en blanco debe obtener la configuración de red vía DHCP al "
"arrancar. La asignación de IP estática no es posible."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:11
msgid "Hypervisor Console must be enabled on the Target Cloud"
msgstr "La Consola de Hipervisor debe estar habilitada en la Nube de destino"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:12
msgid "Morpheus utilizes VNC to pass the boot script to the VM."
msgstr "Morpheus utiliza VNC para pasar el script de arranque a la VM."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:13
msgid "VM must be able to reach and resolve the Morpheus appliance url over 443"
msgstr ""
"La VM debe poder alcanzar y resolver la url del appliance Morpheus "
"sobre el puerto 443"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:14
msgid "The boot script calls to the Morpheus appliance to get the preseed script."
msgstr ""
"El script de arranque llama al appliance Morpheus para obtener el "
"script preseed."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:18
msgid "Valid Linux iso set for the Virtual Image. Windows is not supported."
msgstr ""
"ISO de Linux válido establecido para la Imagen Virtual. Windows no es "
"compatible."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:16
msgid "The iso can exist in the target cloud or uploaded to Morpheus"
msgstr "El ISO puede existir en la nube de destino o subirse a Morpheus"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:18
msgid "``cloud-init enabled`` must be disabled on the iso Virtual Image settings."
msgstr ""
"``cloud-init enabled`` debe ser disabled on the iso Virtual Image settings."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:20
msgid "Access to target ESXi host(s) over 443 and ESXi hostname dns resolution"
msgstr ""
"Acceso al(los) host(s) ESXi de destino sobre 443 y resolución DNS del "
"nombre de host ESXi"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:21
msgid ""
"Same requirement as Hypervisor Console and Image upload/download to/from "
"vCenter."
msgstr ""
"Mismo requisito que la Consola de Hipervisor y la carga/descarga de "
"imágenes hacia/desde vCenter."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:22
msgid "Valid Boot Script"
msgstr "Script de arranque válido"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:23
msgid "Valid Pre-seed script"
msgstr "Script Pre-seed válido"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:24
msgid "Valid Storage Provider configure for ova export of generated image."
msgstr ""
"Proveedor de almacenamiento válido configurado para la exportación ova "
"de la imagen generada."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:27
msgid "Sample Scripts"
msgstr "Scripts de ejemplo"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:30
msgid "Sample Boot Script"
msgstr "Script de arranque de ejemplo"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:32
msgid "<wait5><tab> text ks=<%=preseedUrl%><enter>"
msgstr "<wait5><pestaña> text ks=<%=preseedUrl%><enter>"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:36
msgid ""
"``<%=preseedUrl%>`` is a Morpheus variable that will populate with the "
"Morpheus appliance url."
msgstr ""
"``<%=preseedUrl%>`` es a Morpheus variable que se populate con el/la "
"Morpheus appliance url."

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:39
msgid "Sample Preseed Script"
msgstr "Script Preseed de ejemplo"

#: ../../tools/image_builder.rst:41
#, python-format
msgid ""
"# CentOS 7.x kickstart file - ks.cfg\n"
"#\n"
"# For more information on kickstart syntax and commands, refer to the\n"
"# CentOS Installation Guide:\n"
"# https://access.redhat.com/documentation/en-"
"US/Red_Hat_Enterprise_Linux/7/html/Installation_Guide/sect-kickstart-"
"syntax.html\n"
"#\n"
"# For testing, you can fire up a local http server temporarily.\n"
"# cd to the directory where this ks.cfg file resides and run the "
"following:\n"
"#    $ python -m SimpleHTTPServer\n"
"# You don't have to restart the server every time you make changes.  "
"Python\n"
"# will reload the file from disk every time.  As long as you save your "
"changes\n"
"# they will be reflected in the next HTTP download.  Then to test with\n"
"# a PXE boot server, enter the following on the PXE boot prompt:\n"
"#    > linux text ks=http://<your_ip>:8000/ks.cfg\n"
"\n"
"# Required settings\n"
"lang en_US.UTF-8\n"
"keyboard us\n"
"rootpw password\n"
"authconfig --enableshadow --enablemd5\n"
"timezone UTC\n"
"\n"
"# Optional settings\n"
"install\n"
"cdrom\n"
"user --name=cloud-user --plaintext --password password\n"
"unsupported_hardware\n"
"network --bootproto=dhcp\n"
"firewall --disabled\n"
"selinux --permissive\n"
"bootloader --location=mbr --append=\"biosdevname=0 net.ifnames=0\"\n"
"text\n"
"skipx\n"
"zerombr\n"
"clearpart --all --initlabel\n"
"autopart --type=plain\n"
"firstboot --disabled\n"
"reboot\n"
"\n"
"%packages --nobase --ignoremissing --excludedocs\n"
"openssh-clients\n"
"# Prerequisites for installing VMware Tools guest additions.\n"
"# Put in kickstart to ensure first version installed is from install "
"disk,\n"
"# not latest from a mirror.\n"
"kernel-headers\n"
"kernel-devel\n"
"gcc\n"
"make\n"
"perl\n"
"curl\n"
"wget\n"
"bzip2\n"
"dkms\n"
"patch\n"
"net-tools\n"
"git\n"
"# Core selinux dependencies installed on 7.x, no need to specify\n"
"# Other stuff\n"
"sudo\n"
"nfs-utils\n"
"open-vm-tools\n"
"-fprintd-pam\n"
"-intltool\n"
"-biosdevname\n"
"\n"
"# unnecessary firmware\n"
"-aic94xx-firmware\n"
"-atmel-firmware\n"
"-b43-openfwwf\n"
"-bfa-firmware\n"
"-ipw*-firmware\n"
"-irqbalance\n"
"-ivtv-firmware\n"
"-iwl*-firmware\n"
"-libertas-usb8388-firmware\n"
"-ql*-firmware\n"
"-rt61pci-firmware\n"
"-rt73usb-firmware\n"
"-xorg-x11-drv-ati-firmware\n"
"-zd1211-firmware\n"
"%end\n"
"\n"
"%post\n"
"# configure vagrant user in sudoers\n"
"echo \"%cloud-user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL\" >> /etc/sudoers.d/cloud-user"
"\n"
"chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/cloud-user\n"
"cp /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.orig\n"
"sed -i \"s/^\\(.*requiretty\\)$/#\\1/\" /etc/sudoers\n"
"# keep proxy settings through sudo\n"
"echo 'Defaults env_keep += \"HTTP_PROXY HTTPS_PROXY FTP_PROXY RSYNC_PROXY"
" NO_PROXY\"' >> /etc/sudoers\n"
"%end"
msgstr ""
"# CentOS 7.x kickstart file - ks.cfg\n#\n# For more information on "
"kickstart syntax and commands, refer to the\n# CentOS Installation "
"Guide:\n# https://access.redhat.com/documentation/en-US/Red_Hat_Enterprise_"
"Linux/7/html/Installation_Guide/sect-kickstart-syntax.html\n#\n# For "
"testing, you can fire up a local http server temporarily.\n# cd to the "
"directory where this ks.cfg file resides and run the following:\n#    $ "
"python -m SimpleHTTPServer\n# You don't have to restart the server every "
"time you make changes.  Python\n# will reload the file from disk every "
"time.  As long as you save your changes\n# they will be reflected in the "
"next HTTP download.  Then to test with\n# a PXE boot server, enter the "
"following on the PXE boot prompt:\n#    > linux text "
"ks=http://<your_ip>:8000/ks.cfg\n\n# Required settings\nlang "
"en_US.UTF-8\nkeyboard us\nrootpw password\nauthconfig --enableshadow "
"--enablemd5\ntimezone UTC\n\n# Optional settings\ninstall\ncdrom\nuser "
"--name=cloud-user --plaintext --password "
"password\nunsupported_hardware\nnetwork --bootproto=dhcp\nfirewall "
"--disabled\nselinux --permissive\nbootloader --location=mbr "
"--append=\"biosdevname=0 net.ifnames=0\"\ntext\nskipx\nzerombr\nclearpart "
"--all --initlabel\nautopart --type=plain\nfirstboot "
"--disabled\nreboot\n\n%packages --nobase --ignoremissing "
"--excludedocs\nopenssh-clients\n# Prerequisites for installing VMware "
"Tools guest additions.\n# Put in kickstart to ensure first version "
"installed is from install disk,\n# not latest from a "
"mirror.\nkernel-headers\nkernel-devel\ngcc\nmake\nperl\ncurl\nwget\nbzip2\n"
"dkms\npatch\nnet-tools\ngit\n# Core selinux dependencies installed on 7.x, "
"no need to specify\n# Other "
"stuff\nsudo\nnfs-utils\nopen-vm-tools\n-fprintd-pam\n-intltool\n-biosdevnam"
"e\n\n# unnecessary firmware\n-aic94xx-firmware\n-atmel-firmware\n-b43-openf"
"wwf\n-bfa-firmware\n-ipw*-firmware\n-irqbalance\n-ivtv-firmware\n-iwl*-firm"
"ware\n-libertas-usb8388-firmware\n-ql*-firmware\n-rt61pci-firmware\n-rt73us"
"b-firmware\n-xorg-x11-drv-ati-firmware\n-zd1211-firmware\n%end\n\n%post\n# "
"configure vagrant user in sudoers\necho \"%cloud-user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: "
"ALL\" >> /etc/sudoers.d/cloud-user\nchmod 0440 "
"/etc/sudoers.d/cloud-user\ncp /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.orig\nsed -i "
"\"s/^\\(.*requiretty\\)$/#\\1/\" /etc/sudoers\n# keep proxy settings "
"through sudo\necho 'Defaults env_keep += \"HTTP_PROXY HTTPS_PROXY "
"FTP_PROXY RSYNC_PROXY NO_PROXY\"' >> /etc/sudoers\n%end"

